WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.619
The picture can drive the synth, too.

2
00:00:02.619 --> 00:00:06.458
Video nodes measure brightness, motion, color and edges in the live image.

3
00:00:06.913 --> 00:00:07.834
Add Video Luma.

4
00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:10.721
It reports how bright a region of the frame is.

5
00:00:11.173 --> 00:00:14.304
Drag on the thumbnail in the inspector to choose the region.

6
00:00:14.304 --> 00:00:16.234
Here, the moving shape in the middle.

7
00:00:16.698 --> 00:00:17.688
Bind it to Z Push.

8
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:20.273
Now the depth follows that part of the picture.

9
00:00:20.728 --> 00:00:23.722
Video Motion measures how much the image is changing.

10
00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:26.207
Smooth it with a Slew, and send it to Bloom.

11
00:00:34.561 --> 00:00:39.855
The Library has more: Motion-Triggered Glitch tears the raster whenever something moves.

12
00:00:40.305 --> 00:00:41.315
Restore the window.

13
00:00:41.315 --> 00:00:43.230
The camera is now playing the synth.

14
00:00:44.994 --> 00:00:49.560
Point a webcam at a dancer, a lava lamp, or your own hands.

15
00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.031
Next: MIDI and OSC.
